### Configure Extras for Whitespace and Comments in Tree-sitter

Source: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter/blob/master/docs/src/creating-parsers/3-writing-the-grammar.md

This JavaScript snippet shows how to define 'extras' in a Tree-sitter grammar, allowing tokens like whitespace and comments to appear anywhere. It associates patterns with rules for better performance and maintainability.

```javascript
module.exports = grammar({
  name: "my_language",

  extras: ($) => [
    /\s/, // whitespace
    $.comment,
  ],

  rules: {
    comment: ($) =>
      token(
        choice(seq("//", /.*/), seq("/*", /[^*]*\*+([^/*][^*]*\*+)*/, "/")),
      ),
  },
});
```

